{
    "background_story": "Lillie was a free-spirited artist known for her extravagant lifestyle. She had a habit of spending money lavishly on art supplies, fancy clothes, and luxurious getaways. Her friends and family would often warn her about her wasteful ways, but Lillie couldn't resist the thrill of indulging in life's finer things. Her studio was a testament to her excesses, filled with half-finished canvases, discarded materials, and expensive gadgets that she would use once and then forget. Despite her wasteful tendencies, Lillie's art was highly sought after, and she was able to justify her spending as 'investing in her creativity.' However, as the years went by, Lillie began to realize that her reckless spending was taking a toll on her finances and her relationships. She slowly started to make amends, adopting a more mindful approach to her art and her life.",
